                    <h2 id="programs-attendance-POSTapi-attendances-qr">Mark attendance with a QR token.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Requires permission: <code>participant.qr.use</code>. The QR token can be the raw token or a scanned URL containing <code>token</code>. If the program has coordinates, latitude and longitude are required and checked against the configured radius.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-attendances-qr">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/attendances/qr" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"qr_token\": \"qr_abc123\",
    \"latitude\": 41.0082,
    \"longitude\": 28.9784
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/attendances/qr"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "qr_token": "qr_abc123",
    "latitude": 41.0082,
    "longitude": 28.9784
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

</span>

<span id="example-responses-POSTapi-attendances-qr">
