                    <h2 id="requests-GETapi-requests--id--response-file">Download a workflow request response file.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>The requester can download their response file. Panel users can download when they can manage the request through <code>requests.view</code>, <code>requests.upload_response</code>, or <code>requests.update_status</code>. Returns a storage direct URL when configured; otherwise streams the binary file. Downloads are audit logged.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-requests--id--response-file">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/requests/1/response-file" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json"</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
