                    <h2 id="announcements-inbox-PUTapi-admin-announcements--id-">Update a panel announcement.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Requires permission: <code>announcements.update</code> and access to the announcement. Completed periods require archive update permission. Project changes are checked against the caller project scope; removing the project link is only allowed with global scope. Target units are validated against the caller unit targets.</p>

<span id="example-requests-PUTapi-admin-announcements--id-">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request PUT \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/admin/announcements/1" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"title\": \"Guncel duyuru\",
    \"content\": \"Guncellenen duyuru metni.\",
    \"category\": \"general\",
    \"target_roles\": [
        \"student\",
        \"alumni\"
    ],
    \"target_units\": [
        \"program\"
    ],
    \"project_id\": 1,
    \"period_id\": 3,
    \"published_at\": \"2026-07-01 09:00:00\",
    \"expires_at\": \"2026-07-31 23:59:00\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/admin/announcements/1"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "title": "Guncel duyuru",
