                    <h2 id="permissions-matrix-PUTapi-panel-permissions-matrix-users--id-">Update user permission overrides.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Requires permission: <code>permissions.user_override.update</code> with global <code>all</code> scope. Replaces all overrides for the target user. Permission names must exist in the granular catalog or legacy map, must be compatible with the user role and scope types must be allowed for the role/permission pair. Clears the permission cache and logs <code>user_permission_overrides.updated</code>.</p>

<span id="example-requests-PUTapi-panel-permissions-matrix-users--id-">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request PUT \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/permissions-matrix/users/8" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"overrides\": [
        \"consequatur\"
    ]
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/permissions-matrix/users/8"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "overrides": [
        "consequatur"
    ]
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "PUT",
    headers,
