                    <h2 id="calendar-GETapi-panel-calendar-assignees">List calendar assignees.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Returns active coordinator/staff users that can be assigned to a program or meeting. Exposed under <code>/panel/calendar/assignees</code> and <code>/calendar/assignees</code>. Permission depends on <code>context</code>: <code>calendar.assignments.manage</code> for program assignments, <code>calendar.meetings.create</code> for meeting creation, and <code>calendar.meetings.manage</code> for meeting management.</p>
<p>If <code>project_id</code> is provided, the caller must have that permission for the project. General meetings without a project require global scope for the selected meeting permission. Media-unit staff may be assignable across projects; other candidates must coordinate, participate in, or have calendar/projects access to the project.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-panel-calendar-assignees">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/assignees?project_id=3&amp;context=meeting_create" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"project_id\": 17,
    \"context\": \"program\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/assignees"
);

const params = {
    "project_id": "3",
    "context": "meeting_create",
};
Object.keys(params)
    .forEach(key =&gt; url.searchParams.append(key, params[key]));

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "project_id": 17,
    "context": "program"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "GET",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

</span>

