                    <h2 id="calendar-GETapi-panel-calendar-google-connect">Create a Google Calendar OAuth URL.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Exposed under <code>/panel/calendar/google/connect</code> and <code>/calendar/google/connect</code>. Requires global <code>all</code> scope for <code>calendar.google.connect</code>. Generates a short-lived OAuth state and returns the Google authorization URL. The callback is handled outside the API controller by the Google Calendar callback route.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-panel-calendar-google-connect">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/google/connect?panel=admin" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
    --data "{
    \"panel\": \"coordinator\"
}"
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/google/connect"
);

const params = {
    "panel": "admin",
};
Object.keys(params)
    .forEach(key =&gt; url.searchParams.append(key, params[key]));

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};

let body = {
    "panel": "coordinator"
};

fetch(url, {
    method: "GET",
    headers,
    body: JSON.stringify(body),
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

