                    <h2 id="calendar-POSTapi-panel-calendar-google-sync">Sync programs to Google Calendar.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Exposed under <code>/panel/calendar/google/sync</code> and <code>/calendar/google/sync</code>. Requires global <code>all</code> scope for <code>calendar.google.sync</code>. Synchronizes all non-completed-period programs into local <code>CalendarEvent</code> rows and, when Google is configured and connected, creates or updates events in the configured Google calendar.</p>
<p>Google API/token failures are recorded into system settings as the last sync error and returned as validation/API errors by the service.</p>

<span id="example-requests-POSTapi-panel-calendar-google-sync">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request POST \
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/google/sync" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json"</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/google/sync"
);

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};


fetch(url, {
    method: "POST",
    headers,
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

</span>

