                    <h2 id="calendar-GETapi-panel-calendar-export">Export calendar programs.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Exposed under <code>/panel/calendar/export</code>. Requires <code>calendar.export</code>. Global scope exports all projects; project-scoped users are limited to projects returned by <code>calendar.export</code>. Optional project and period filters narrow the exported program rows. Manual meetings are not included in this export; the file contains program calendar rows with Google sync and assignment columns.</p>
<p>Supported file formats are handled by <code>AdminExportResponder</code> through the <code>format</code> query parameter and default to CSV.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-panel-calendar-export">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/export?project_id=3&amp;period_id=12&amp;format=xlsx" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/panel/calendar/export"
);

const params = {
    "project_id": "3",
    "period_id": "12",
    "format": "xlsx",
};
Object.keys(params)
    .forEach(key =&gt; url.searchParams.append(key, params[key]));

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};


fetch(url, {
    method: "GET",
    headers,
}).then(response =&gt; response.json());</code></pre></div>

</span>

