                    <h2 id="calendar-GETapi-calendar-overview">Get the calendar overview.</h2>

<p>
<small class="badge badge-darkred">requires authentication</small>
</p>

<p>Returns the panel calendar timeline for programs and manual meetings. Exposed under <code>/panel/calendar/overview</code> and <code>/calendar/overview</code>. Requires <code>calendar.view</code>; project/period filters are resolved through the shared project-period context. Non-global users are limited by their calendar scope, assigned meeting records, or records they created. The system may allow coordinator/staff cross-project calendar visibility for conflict checks via <code>permission_catalog.calendar_cross_project_view_for_staff_coordinator</code>.</p>
<p>The response includes available projects with active period, merged program/meeting items, upcoming tasks, attention items for unassigned or unsynced events, support counters, and Google Calendar connection status.</p>

<span id="example-requests-GETapi-calendar-overview">
<blockquote>Example request:</blockquote>


<div class="bash-example">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">curl --request GET \
    --get "http://localhost:8000/api/calendar/overview?project_id=3&amp;period_id=12" \
    --header "Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}" \
    --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
    --header "Accept: application/json" \
</code></pre></div>


<div class="javascript-example">
    <pre><code class="language-javascript">const url = new URL(
    "http://localhost:8000/api/calendar/overview"
);

const params = {
    "project_id": "3",
    "period_id": "12",
};
Object.keys(params)
    .forEach(key =&gt; url.searchParams.append(key, params[key]));

const headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer {YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN}",
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "Accept": "application/json",
};


fetch(url, {
